<headroom-library version="1" id="hg-low-tuned-brutality" category="High Gain" order="90" instrument="guitar" style="Death Metal">
  <description>Brutal death metal for B, A and lower: an overdrive tightens a rectified head and a 120-watt lead channel blended underneath, both into a Greenback 4x12, with a hard gate. Scooped and huge but tight in the lows, so blasts, slams and low-string chugs stay articulate.</description>
  <tags><tag>High Gain</tag><tag>Death Metal</tag><tag>Brutal</tag><tag>Rhythm</tag><tag>Downtuned</tag><tag>Gate</tag><tag>Layered</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://www.premierguitar.com/artists/guitarists/cannibal-corpses-violence-unimagined-new-guitarist-classic-sound" title="Premier Guitar: Cannibal Corpse's Violence Unimagined"/>
    <source url="https://www.premierguitar.com/artists/is-erik-rutan-death-metals-renaissance-man" title="Premier Guitar: Is Erik Rutan death metal's renaissance man?"/>
    <source url="https://www.decibelmagazine.com/2021/10/08/suffocation-death-metal/" title="Decibel: Suffocation, Effigy of the Forgotten"/>
    <source url="https://sevenstring.org/threads/some-sample-settings-for-an-808-in-front-of-a-5150.143177/" title="Sevenstring.org: sample settings for an 808 in front of a 5150 (forum)"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
